    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2607.27472v1</id>
    <title>The stochastic Keller--Segel system in critical spaces</title>
    <updated>2026-07-29T21:24:40Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.27472v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.27472v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We study stochastic, parabolic-parabolic Keller--Segel equations on the $d$-dimensional torus in scaling critical Besov spaces, for $d \geq 3$. Using stochastic maximal regularity estimates, we prove local well-posedness of the equation, i.e., that there exists a unique solution up to a maximal time of existence. We show that the time of existence can be made arbitrarily large with arbitrarily high probability, provided that the initial data is sufficiently small in these critical spaces.
  Contribution to the Oberwolfach Report for the Seminar 'Stochastic Partial Differential Equations in Critical Spaces' organized by Antonio Agresti and Mark Veraar.</summary>
    <category term="math.PR" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
